Memory capacity is becoming an increasingly important consideration as organizations deploy AI infrastructure, cloud platforms, enterprise servers and memory-intensive workstations. Dual in-line memory modules (DIMMs) package DRAM chips on standardized circuit boards that connect directly to a system's memory interface. They allow manufacturers and system integrators to configure, upgrade and service system memory according to workload requirements.

